# PharmaGuard backend — environment template.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Nothing here is required for the deployed path.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit a real key.

# --- Explanations -----------------------------------------------------------
# static   (default, deployed) serve pre-generated, guard-checked explanations.
#          No API call, no key. This is what production runs.
# live     compatibility mode; approved static content or deterministic fallback.
#          Runtime clinical prose is not generated.
# template deterministic composition only.
EXPLANATION_MODE=static

# Safe default: ignore caller-supplied forwarding headers. Set only to direct
# proxy IP/CIDR ranges that sanitize X-Forwarded-For, and align uvicorn's
# forwarded-header trust with the same boundary.
TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=

# --- Optional: live mode / offline pre-generation ----------------------------
# Read by offline pre-generation scripts only. The request path makes no
# outbound model call in any explanation mode.
# Free tier available at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Override the model id. Default is set in app/explanation/generator_llm.py
# (checked against ai.google.dev on 2026-07-22).
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# --- Paths (usually auto-detected) ------------------------------------------
# Where the mechanism corpus lives. Set in the Docker image because the
# container layout differs from the repo layout.
# PHARMAGUARD_CORPUS_DIR=/opt/pharmaguard/rag-corpus/mechanisms

# Where guard violations are appended as JSONL.
# GUARD_LOG_PATH=logs/guard_violations.jsonl

# --- PharmCAT ---------------------------------------------------------------
# PHARMCAT_PIPELINE=pharmcat_pipeline
# PHARMCAT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# PHARMCAT_TERMINATION_GRACE_SECONDS=2

# --- Deployment (Phase 4) ----------------------------------------------------
# Exact origins allowed to call this API from a browser, comma-separated.
# NO WILDCARD.
#
# SET THIS LOCALLY TOO. `assert_cors_configured` refuses to start when hosting
# markers (PORT, K_SERVICE, SPACE_ID, RENDER) are present and this is empty —
# that guard exists because an unset allowlist passes every health check while
# blocking every real browser request. Leaving it empty in development means
# local startup takes a DIFFERENT path from production, so the one configuration
# that matters is the one never exercised. Setting the localhost origins here
# converges the two.
#
# The backend does not auto-load this file — export it:
#     set -a && source backend/.env && set +a
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080,http://127.0.0.1:8080,http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000

# On the deployed backend, replace the above with your frontend's exact origin:
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://pharmaguard.pages.dev

# Cloudflare Pages project name, to also allow its per-branch preview
# subdomains (<hash>.<project>.pages.dev). Scoped to one project — never
# a blanket *.pages.dev, which any attacker could deploy under.
# CORS_ALLOW_PAGES_PREVIEWS=pharmaguard

# Shared public workload budget for /coverage and /analyze. Analysis spawns a
# JVM; preview still performs bounded decompression and parsing.
# RATE_LIMIT_REQUESTS=10
# RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS=300

# Injected by Cloud Run and Render. The container falls back to 7860
# (the Hugging Face Spaces convention) when unset.
# PORT=8080
